{"id": "section-body-29228", "title": "Psoriatic Arthritis (PsA)", "chapterId": "chapter-twenty-six", "tocLevel": 4, "tocPath": ["APPROACH TO PATIENTS WITH EMERGENCY CONDITIONS", "RHEUMATOLOGICAL DISORDERS", "Inflammatory Arthritis", "Psoriatic Arthritis (PsA)"], "blocks": [{"id": "body-29228", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Psoriatic Arthritis (PsA)", "runs": [{"text": "Psoriatic"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Arthritis"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(PsA)"}], "level": 4, "list": {"level": 2, "numberingId": "105"}}, {"id": "body-29229", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "PsA is a chronic inflammatory arthritis that is usually seen in patients with psoriasis, although it may predate skin involvement, which can be subtle. It typically presents as seronegative oligoarthritic, with features such as distal joint involvement, arthritis mutilans, or inflammation of joints, spine, entheses, nails, and skin.", "runs": [{"text": "PsA"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "chronic"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "inflammatory"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "arthritis"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "that"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "usually"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "seen"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "in"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "patients"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "with"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "psoriasis,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "although"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "it"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "may"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "predate"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "skin"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "involvement, which can be subtle. It typically presents as seronegative oligoarthritic, with features such as distal joint involvement, arthritis mutilans, or inflammation of joints, spine, entheses, nails, and skin."}]}, {"id": "body-29231", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Clinical Presentation", "runs": [{"text": "Clinical"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Presentation"}]